                <pb facs="0808" n="716" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg716"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/11099</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shea</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-26T00:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 26, 1918, 12 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5.21 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Embassy’s telegram of August 9, 2 p.m. Much activity in official quarters. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">La Nacion</hi>, controlled by Señor Yanez, in leading
                    editorial yesterday urges action be taken to acquire German ships. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mercurio</hi> of this morning has editorial on the same
                    lines. Am of opinion that a direct intimation that it will be necessary very
                    soon to divert the <hi rendition="#italic">Santa Ana</hi> and one or two British
                    vessels from west coast trade would have good effect and might bring quick
                    settlement. For good of local conditions intimation should be made quickly. It
                    will also help the situation if it is intimated that hereafter our ships will be
                    devoted to nitrate trade exclusively and will therefore not come south of
                    Antofagasta.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shea</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
